# TARGET ARCHITECTURE: aarch64 (ARM64) | v0.16.2 | gcp/ubuntu2604
# ARM64-specific syscall mapping; reconcile against this product/version ARM64 STIG or approved baseline.
# Enterprise Linux Audit v0.16.2  |  [gcp/ubuntu2604]
# Tier: tier-2-core-security
# Purpose: hostname and local resolver changes
# Source/authority: Enterprise SOC/IR minimum
# Architecture: aarch64 (b64 only). No x86/compat b32 syscall rules.
# Release state: engineering candidate; NOT independently certified STIG compliant.


-a always,exit -F arch=b64 -S sethostname,setdomainname -F auid>=1000 -F auid!=unset -k t2_net_config
-a always,exit -F arch=b64 -F path=/etc/hosts -F perm=wa -k t2_net_config
# OPTIONAL if the file exists (often a symlink or dynamically managed):
# -a always,exit -F arch=b64 -F path=/etc/resolv.conf -F perm=wa -k t2_net_config
# Cloud security-group / NSG / VPC firewall changes occur in cloud control-plane APIs, not here.
